      "title": "Temporary Human Resources Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\n\nLocation: Hastings\n\nPosition Type: Part-Time, Temporary (up to 30 hours per week) Duration: Approximately 12 weeks (Mid-January – Mid-April) Location:  Onsite in Hastings, NE  Flexible Schedule: Up to 30 hours per week. Monday – Friday core working hours are required between 9:00 AM and 2:30 PM with daily schedules agreed upon with the HR Director. Hastings College is seeking a detail-oriented and proactive onsite Temporary HR Assistant to support the Human Resources Department during a team leave of absence. The employment period will be from approximately mid-January to mid-April. The schedule is 30 hours per week with flexible hours. While Hastings College HR operating hours are Monday through Friday, 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM, we offer flexibility on start and end times provided core operational hours (9:00 AM to 2:30 PM) are covered. Reporting directly to the HR Director in a fast-paced, two-person department, this role will be instrumental in managing day-to-day administrative functions, maintaining employee records, supporting HRIS and benefit processes, and delivering exceptional service to Hastings College employees.  Job Summary: Serve as the primary first point of contact for the HR office, triaging inquiries via phone, email, and in-person visits. Maintain accurate and up-to-date employee records, including personnel files and the HRIS. Conduct new hire onboarding, including issuing offer packets, initiating background checks, and tracking Form I-9 completion. Assist with administering employee benefits programs, including health, dental, vision, retirement plans, and leave policies. Escalate any employee relations issues to the Director of Human Resources.  Receive, review, and accurately enter department invoices into ReqLogic. Help maintain HR content on the college internal portal/website. Assist with routine HR compliance auditing and reporting. See the job description for a full list of essential functions.  Education & Experience: Associate’s degree in human resources, business administration, or a related field and at least one year of experience in human resources; or equivalent combination of education and experience. Prior experience using ADP preferred.  Equal Opportunity Employment  Hastings College is committed to supporting a welcoming academic and employment environment. The College is an Equal Opportunity employer that does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, national origin, religion, age, sex, marital status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by local, state, or federal laws. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States. This position is not eligible for work visa sponsorship now or in the future.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=47560b19-b691-4f4c-9de8-ff510ff2a256&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=274392338538_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Criminology, Criminal Justice, or Sociology Faculty (Open Rank)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\n\nLocation: Hastings\n\nHastings College is seeking a full-time Criminology, Criminal Justice, or Sociology faculty member to begin in August 2027. Rank is open (tenure or non-tenure) and will be contingent upon the selected candidate's educational background, teaching experience, and scholarly achievements, subject to final determination by the Vice President for Academic Affairs. Experience in providing leadership for curriculum development and interdepartmental collaboration will be strongly considered. Qualifications: Master’s degree in Criminology, Criminal Justice, Sociology, or a related field is required; PhD preferred but will also consider Master's degree candidates  with relevant industry, technical, or applied professional background. Responsibilities: Teach a variety of Criminology, Criminal Justice, Sociology courses to departmental majors, other majors, and in the general education curriculum. Instruct within the block schedule, utilizing 8-week terms to facilitate focused, immersive learning. Serve as an academic advisor to students. Contribute to departmental and institutional initiatives. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS   The successful candidate will hold a Maters degree in Criminology, Criminal Justice, Sociology or a related field; PhD is preferred.  Demonstrated teaching experience is required, either concurrent to, or following graduate studies.  The ability to work well as a member of a department and campus community at liberal arts college is essential.    Qualified candidates need to complete the online application and download into the profile section of the online application; a cover letter, a statement of teaching philosophy, curriculum vitae (CV) which includes the contact information for three references, and unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts.  Application Deadline: October 30, 2026 HASTINGS COLLEGE–  Founded in 1882, Hastings College is dedicated to the liberal arts educational model that prepares students to be citizens and leaders of their communities. Our education builds the innate talents of each student through impactful real-world experiences and universal curriculum to maximize their personal and career success in an ever-changing world. We have an enrollment of around 900, a student-to-faculty ratio of 14:1 and are housed on 120 beautiful acres. Hastings, Nebraska, population 25,000, is a supportive community with a multitude of amenities MISSION – Formed through exceptional teaching, deliberate mentoring, welcoming and participatory community, Hastings College sends forth creative, curious, caring students who thrive as citizens and leaders of their local and global communities.    HASTINGS, NEBRASKA–  Hastings, Nebraska is an attractive residential community located in the heart of south central Nebraska in a metro area that includes the cities of Grand Island and Kearney. Hastings is two and a half hours west of Omaha, six hours east of Denver and five hours northwest of Kansas City. The city enjoys excellent public and private schools, offers numerous professional and community services, and serves as a cultural center for a large surrounding area. Equal Employment Opportunity Hastings College is committed to supporting a welcoming academic and employment environment. The College is an Equal Opportunity employer that does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, national origin, religion, age, sex, marital status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by local, state, or federal laws. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States. This position is not eligible for work visa sponsorship now or in the future.",
