      "title": "Women's Basketball Assistant Coach (Part-Time)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-03\n\nLocation: Hastings\n\nHastings College is accepting applications for the position of Part-time Assistant Coach for Women’s Basketball. This role include coaching a position, recruiting student-athletes to Hastings College, and representing the college, athletic department and Basketball program in a positive manner.  This position reports to the Head Women’s Basketball Coach.  Qualified applicants need to complete the online application, current resume, and contact information for three references in the profile section of the online application. Applications will be accepted until the position has been filled. Responsibilities Support the philosophy, mission, and standards of Hastings College, the Great Plains Athletic Conference (GPAC), and the NAIA. Coaching the Junior Varsity Team.  Assist in developing and maintain a highly competitive intercollegiate program within rules and regulations of the institution, the GPAC and NAIA. Assist in planning, organizing and managing all phases of the program including: teaching student-athlete skill development and mental/motivating techniques for competition, scheduling and supervision of practice and game sessions, supervision of support staff members in an efficient and productive manner monitoring and maintaining the discipline and conduct of student-athletes to support the image and reputation of the athletics program. Recruit and retain academically qualified student-athletes within the guidelines of Hastings College, the Great Plains Athletic Conference (GPAC), and the NAIA. Maintain a roster that is competitive within the GPAC and NAIA and support the college enrollment strategy/mission.  Monitor student-athlete progression to ensure graduation, retention, and eligibility.  Work cooperatively with faculty members, admission, alumni, and development office personnel, the sports information director, all student support services, and all athletic department personnel.   Education & Experience for the Part-Time Assistant Coach  Bachelor's degree preferred.  Previous experience playing at the collegiate level or two years previous experience coaching.    Equal Opportunity Employment  Hastings College is committed to supporting a welcoming academic and employment environment. The College is an Equal Opportunity employer that does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, national origin, religion, age, sex, marital status, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by local, state, or federal laws. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States. This position is not eligible for work visa sponsorship now or in the future.",
      "department": ""
    },
